{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1444526-aberrant-variable-x-tag-examples","id":1444526,"title":"[Aberrant] Variable (X) Tag: examples","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","The Trinity Continuum","Trinity Continuum: Aberrant"],"posts":[{"date":"2021-04-18T11:22:23-07:00","id":1444526,"title":"[Aberrant] Variable (X) Tag: examples","content":"<span style=\"font-size:16px\">Variable (X) Tag: examples</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Could you please give some concrete and elucidative examples of the use of this tag? (Aberrant p 204). Thank you!!!</span></span></span></span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1001-timecrafter","name":"Timecrafter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1001_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"134"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-18T13:34:33-07:00","id":1444539,"title":"","content":"Imagine someone with the Quantum Attack power, one based on electricity. Quantum Attack provides points for tags equal to its rating, so we don't have to worry about how to acquire that. That person wants to have a taser power, but they <i>also</i> want to toss around a lightning bolt. Rather than splurge for multiple instances of Quantum Attack, they just use their QA tag points for the Variable Tag. With QA 2, they can have 2 1-dot Tags they can switch between: a Close-Range Attack with the Stun (1) tag (for the taser), and a Low-Range (1) lightning bolt. With QA 3, they can have either 2 2-dot Tags they can swap between, or 3 1-dot Tags. For the 2 2-dot tags: Either a Low-Range (1) Attack with Stun (1) or a Non-Lethal (2) Attack (for the taser), and a Medium-Range (2) lightning bolt or Low-Range (1) Electrical (1) Attack. For the 3 1-dot tags: The first two examples, plus maybe a more lethal Close Range Attack with Electrical (1). Sorry if that's a bit of a text wall, but these are all things you can do with just one concept for Quantum Attack, let alone some of the other powers.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26317-critian-caceorte","name":"Critian Caceorte","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"246"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-18T14:12:21-07:00","id":1444545,"title":"","content":"Just to make it more clear (it took me 3 reads to understand you are correct). I made 3 examples, 1 basic QAttack 2, 1 with 1 alternative of 2 tags and 1 with 2 alternatives of 1 tag<br /> <br /> Quantum Attack 2 : Variable (2 - 1 for 1 alternative and 1 for 1 tag that change)<br /> Teaser - Stun (1)<br /> Lighting bolt - Shot range (1)<br /> <br /> Quantum Attack 3 : Variable (3 - 1 for 1 alternative and 2 for 2 tags that change)<br /> Teaser - Stun (1) Short Range (1) <br /> Lighting bolt - Short range (1) Electrical (1)<br /> <br /> Quantum Attack 3 : Variable (3 - 2 for 2 alternative and 1 for 1 tags that change)<br /> Teaser - Stun (1) <br /> Lighting bolt - Short range (1)<br /> Electrical Touch - Electrical (1)<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-19T05:55:29-07:00","id":1444637,"title":"","content":"<i>(Variable (X), Aberrant p.204)<br /> &quot;A power with this tag actually has multiple tags or combinations of tags it can switch between, changing from one configuration to another. Choose the maximum points in tags the power can have at any one time (including reducing costs for negative tags, minimum 0) and add one per additional configuration the power can switch to. A power can have Variable tags as well as fixed tags, such as a power that always has Charging but also a set of Variable tags. In this case, the fixed tags are not counted towards the dots in Variable tags. Free tags provided by the power\u2019s dots are always considered fixed and not Variable.&quot;</i><br /> <br /> 0) I started to read your examples, but -- correct-me if I'm wrong -- you are not using &quot;<i>Free tags provided by the power\u2019s dots are always considered fixed and not Variable.&quot;</i>&quot;, right?<br /> <br /> 1) My main question is: do each power configuration must be pre-defined, or can I substitute them dynamically during the adventure (as long as I respect the level and quantity restrictions I bought)?<br /> <br /> In other words, does &quot;MyQuantumPower Variable(X)&quot;, that I bought with the restrictions &quot;no more than 3 tags, and each tag at most can be level 2&quot; takes &quot;one configuration slot&quot; for <i>each </i>combination of tags (I choose each Tag during character creation, and CANNOT change them), or &quot;one configuration slot&quot; for <i>all</i> (I choose the Tags each time I use the power, my only limitation is the &quot;maximum tag level&quot;)?<br /> <br /> 2) My second question is: if my choices of tags are made only during character creation, and I cant change them, why would I use the &quot;Variable(X) Tag&quot; if I can do the same thing using &quot;Technique&quot; Mega-Edge???<br /> <br /> These are some reasons I'd like to understand what the Devs intended. :/<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1001-timecrafter","name":"Timecrafter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1001_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"134"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-19T07:17:47-07:00","id":1444656,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Timecrafter</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1444526-aberrant-variable-x-tag-examples?p=1444637#post1444637\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">0) I started to read your examples, but -- correct-me if I'm wrong -- you are not using &quot;<i>Free tags provided by the power\u2019s dots are always considered fixed and not Variable.&quot;</i>&quot;, right?<br /> <br /> 1) My main question is: do each power configuration must be pre-defined, or can I substitute them dynamically during the adventure (as long as I respect the level and quantity restrictions I bought)?<br /> <br /> In other words, does &quot;MyQuantumPower Variable(X)&quot;, that I bought with the restrictions &quot;no more than 3 tags, and each tag at most can be level 2&quot; takes &quot;one configuration slot&quot; for <i>each </i>combination of tags (I choose each Tag during character creation, and CANNOT change them), or &quot;one configuration slot&quot; for <i>all</i> (I choose the Tags each time I use the power, my only limitation is the &quot;maximum tag level&quot;)?<br /> <br /> 2) My second question is: if my choices of tags are made only during character creation, and I cant change them, why would I use the &quot;Variable(X) Tag&quot; if I can do the same thing using &quot;Technique&quot; Mega-Edge???<br /> <br /> These are some reasons I'd like to understand what the Devs intended. :/</div> </div> </div> </div>0) indeed. The examples need extra tags, but they are workable.<br /> <br /> 1) It must be pre-defined. It talks about 1 dot cost for each configuration the power can switch to, so it should have fixed configifurations.<br /> <br /> 2) Because you may be in the situation you already have too many techniques of the same power, for example, you have Q4 and already have 5 techniques, so you make your quantum attack a variable tag.<br /> Also, supertech modules can\u2019t have techniques (they have powers or MEdges, but not both), so your versatile Missile launcher need the variable tag.<br /> I know, they are very specific reasons, but yet...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}